cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sourcly in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Sourcly"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Sourcly is an open-source web app that runs entirely in the browser. It searches several
  scholarly databases at once and ranks the results with a transparent, adjustable formula that
  is explained for every result. It labels each source and never hides one unless you filter.
authors:
  - name: "Sourcly"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibrahimomeer/Sourcly"
url: "https://github.com/ibrahimomeer/Sourcly"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.6
keywords:
  - academic search
  - source discovery
  - research tools
  - transparent ranking
